# Repository-wide line-ending and binary-asset policy.
#
# anySSH is built on macOS, Linux and Windows and ships a mix of text sources
# plus binary assets (fonts, icons, the vendored IronRDP WebAssembly module,
# screenshots). Without this file, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`
# would rewrite LF to CRLF on checkout, and Git would happily attempt to
# line-ending-normalise and text-diff binary files.
#
# `text=auto` normalises text to LF in the repository. This is a deliberate
# no-op for the current history: no tracked file contains CRLF (verified with
# `git grep -lI $'\r'` returning zero matches), so adopting this file does not
# rewrite any existing blob. It only prevents regressions going forward.

* text=auto

# --- Fonts -----------------------------------------------------------------
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary

# --- WebAssembly -----------------------------------------------------------
*.wasm   binary

# --- Icons and images ------------------------------------------------------
*.icns   binary
*.ico    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.bmp    binary

# --- Archives and installer payloads --------------------------------------
*.zip    binary
*.gz     binary
*.tar    binary
*.7z     binary
*.dmg    binary
*.exe    binary
*.msi    binary
*.deb    binary
*.rpm    binary
*.sig    binary

# --- Generated files -------------------------------------------------------
# Keep lockfiles out of language statistics and diff-noise review.
pnpm-lock.yaml  linguist-generated=true
Cargo.lock      linguist-generated=true
